                            <comment id="15907333" author="karup1990" created="Mon, 13 Mar 2017 12:02:39 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/ViewProfile.jspa?name=Tagar&quot; class=&quot;user-hover&quot; rel=&quot;Tagar&quot;&gt;Tagar&lt;/a&gt; This was tested against spark standalone mode.&lt;br/&gt;
The logic for url  generation  is  here(&lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/apache/zeppelin/pull/1663/files#diff-dbda0c4083ad9c59ff05f0273b5e760fR186&quot; class=&quot;external-link&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noopener&quot;&gt;https://github.com/apache/zeppelin/pull/1663/files#diff-dbda0c4083ad9c59ff05f0273b5e760fR186&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;br/&gt;
I am not familiar with how this is generated in YARN mode(also not sure if CDH has something specific as well).&lt;br/&gt;
Any pointers would be helpful. &lt;/p&gt;
</comment>
                            <comment id="15926425" author="tagar" created="Wed, 15 Mar 2017 16:02:34 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;Thanks for the follow up &lt;a href=&quot;https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/ViewProfile.jspa?name=karup1990&quot; class=&quot;user-hover&quot; rel=&quot;karup1990&quot;&gt;karup1990&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;I ended up opening a support case with Cloudera.&lt;br/&gt;
Issue turns to be on YARN side: &lt;a href=&quot;https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/YARN-4820&quot; title=&quot;ResourceManager web redirects in HA mode drops query parameters&quot; class=&quot;issue-link&quot; data-issue-key=&quot;YARN-4820&quot;&gt;&lt;del&gt;YARN-4820&lt;/del&gt;&lt;/a&gt; and &lt;a href=&quot;https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/YARN-5246&quot; title=&quot;NMWebAppFilter web redirects drop query parameters&quot; class=&quot;issue-link&quot; data-issue-key=&quot;YARN-5246&quot;&gt;&lt;del&gt;YARN-5246&lt;/del&gt;&lt;/a&gt; both are fixed in Hadoop 2.8 and backported to CDH 5.8.4.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Once we upgrade I can confirm this issue as resolved, but I will close this jira now as issue is not on Zeppelin side.&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="16010786" author="tagar" created="Mon, 15 May 2017 16:22:39 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;Just for the record and to help if anybody else runs into the same issue, &lt;br/&gt;
upgrading to CDH 5.10 / Spark 2.1 still does not fix the issue.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;This is still an active problem for us.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Here&apos;s explanation from Cloudera:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;preformatted panel&quot; style=&quot;border-width: 1px;&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;preformattedContent panelContent&quot;&gt;
&lt;pre&gt;Spark rewrites all query parameters into paths, you can see this if you start up the spark-shell in local mode, 
run a few actions and then use query parameters: 

http://&amp;lt;fqdn&amp;gt;:4040/jobs/job?id=1 will be rewritten to http://&amp;lt;fqdn&amp;gt;:4040/jobs/job/?id=1 

http://&amp;lt;fqdn&amp;gt;:4040/stages/stage?id=1&amp;amp;attempt=0 will be rewritten to http://&amp;lt;fqdn&amp;gt;:4040/stages/stage/?id=1&amp;amp;attempt=0 

This works fine when not running on Yarn. 
The way YARN manages security and auth are through a proxy, the spark Web UI runs a filter,
 org.apache.hadoop.yarn.server.webproxy.amfilter.AmIpFilter, 
which redirects all queries that don&apos;t come from the proxy server to that proxy server, 
and the rewriting done by Spark does not work with query parameters when the AmIpFilter is used. 
This filter is also responsible for constructing the URL&apos;s used in the Spark UI to go 
through the proxy when running on Yarn, for example: 

http://&amp;lt;fqdn&amp;gt;:8088/proxy/application_1494764051826_0002/jobs/job?id=0 

Going directly through the proxy is what works, in terms of handling query parameters correctly today. 
&lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;p&gt;We&apos;re trying to understand what it takes to fix this problem.&lt;br/&gt;
Spark job links still don&apos;t work from Zeppelin.&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="16012889" author="tagar" created="Tue, 16 May 2017 18:36:57 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;although this seems to be broken on Spark on YARN side, still reopening in case if there is any workaround possible on Zeppelin side.&lt;br/&gt;
&lt;a href=&quot;https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/SPARK-20772&quot; title=&quot;Add support for query parameters in redirects on Yarn&quot; class=&quot;issue-link&quot; data-issue-key=&quot;SPARK-20772&quot;&gt;&lt;del&gt;SPARK-20772&lt;/del&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="16458278" author="jongyoul" created="Mon, 30 Apr 2018 02:36:26 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;I think we need to handle this issue in Zeppelin side, too, especially in Yarn mode.&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="16459461" author="tagar" created="Tue, 1 May 2018 05:27:58 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/ViewProfile.jspa?name=jongyoul&quot; class=&quot;user-hover&quot; rel=&quot;jongyoul&quot;&gt;jongyoul&lt;/a&gt;,&#160;&lt;a href=&quot;https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/YARN-6615&quot; title=&quot;AmIpFilter drops query parameters on redirect&quot; class=&quot;issue-link&quot; data-issue-key=&quot;YARN-6615&quot;&gt;&lt;del&gt;YARN-6615&lt;/del&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&#160;fixed this issue for us. yarn proxy was dropping job id and it was causing this.&#160;Are you seeing some other issue?&#160;&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="16459531" author="jongyoul" created="Tue, 1 May 2018 08:36:00 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;Yes, it&#8217;s fixed with the latest yarn versions. But the other old versions&lt;br/&gt;
have still a same issue. It can help them until they update yarn to the&lt;br/&gt;
latest version.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;On Tue, May 1, 2018 at 14:28 Ruslan Dautkhanov (JIRA) &amp;lt;jira@apache.org&amp;gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&amp;#8211; &lt;br/&gt;
&#51060;&#51333;&#50676;, Jongyoul Lee, &#26446;&#23447;&#28872;&lt;br/&gt;
&lt;a href=&quot;http://madeng.net&quot; class=&quot;external-link&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noopener&quot;&gt;http://madeng.net&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="16459714" author="tagar" created="Tue, 1 May 2018 14:22:58 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;Got it, makes sense. A workaround for this problem is to remove org.apache.hadoop.yarn.server.webproxy.amfilter.AmIpFilter from yarn config, as described in &lt;a href=&quot;https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/YARN-6615&quot; title=&quot;AmIpFilter drops query parameters on redirect&quot; class=&quot;issue-link&quot; data-issue-key=&quot;YARN-6615&quot;&gt;&lt;del&gt;YARN-6615&lt;/del&gt;&lt;/a&gt; description.&#160;&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
